// §8c's pathological fixture: "a schema where the only path exceeds
// the depth limit." A chain of 30 DISTINCT namespaces (level0 through
// level29), each one's own `view` permission deferring to the next via
// a real tuple-to-userset hop -- no self-reference, no cycle, just a
// genuinely long, unavoidable chain. Only the LAST level has a direct
// `viewer` grant, so the minimum witness length is exactly 30 tuples
// (29 `next` hops plus the final `viewer` grant) -- well past
// `CHECK_MAX_DEPTH`'s own default of 25
// (`src/config/env.ts`). This tool's own search has no depth cap at all
// (a plain exhaustive walk, cycle-safety only), so it finds this witness
// easily -- the real question is what happens next, when the real
// engine (which DOES enforce a depth budget) is asked to confirm it.
// Generated by a one-off script, not hand-typed 30 times -- see
// `test/pathological-depth-limit.test.ts`'s own doc comment for what
// this fixture is used to prove.

namespace level0 {
  relation next: level1

  permission view = next->view
}

namespace level1 {
  relation next: level2

  permission view = next->view
}

namespace level2 {
  relation next: level3

  permission view = next->view
}

namespace level3 {
  relation next: level4

  permission view = next->view
}

